# What GitHub counts as this repository's source, and what it collapses in a diff.
#
# `.yidam` is the knowledge base the computer is written around — the corpus, the
# catalog, the decisions, and under `.vendor` the yidam framework itself. It is
# several hundred committed files and all of it is prose. Left unmarked it
# outweighs everything else and the language bar reads as Markdown, which
# describes the repository as a document rather than as the funding calculator the
# crates and the site actually make it.
#
# `linguist-vendored` excludes a path from the language statistics and collapses it
# by default in a pull request diff. It does not affect the build, and nothing in
# `crates` or `web` reads these files at compile time — the corpus is linked from
# rustdoc by relative path and parsed by the site at build time from its committed
# form, both of which are unchanged by an attribute.
.yidam/** linguist-vendored

# Redundant under the line above, which already matches it, but `.vendor` is the
# one part of `.yidam` that is genuinely someone else's work rather than this
# project's own, and naming it is the point.
.yidam/.vendor/** linguist-vendored
